  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: b6a89d05e624453468952c25d5e9bc8a, type: 2}
  radioLine:
    speaker: Radio
    text: ...Caspian Air regrets to announce that flight 214 to New York is delayed.
      Passengers are asked to remain at their hotels. We will update you at three
      a.m.
  radioReactions:
  - Delayed again. Watch says 3:12. Watch has said 3:12 since Tuesday. Might as well
    read the paper.
  - Same announcement. They must have it on a loop.
  - ...Same words. Same pause before "three a.m."
  - ...
  mirrorLines:
  - Hat brim down. Three days of stubble under there, probably. Don't need to check.
  - Mirror's cold. Cheap hotel.
  - Still haven't slept. Face doesn't look tired. Can't really see the face.
  - Don't feel like looking right now.
  endingLines:
  - speaker: 
    text: Dutch looks.
  - speaker: 
    text: The man in the glass is wearing his coat and his hat, lit the wrong colour.
  - speaker: Reflection
    text: Took you long enough.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: You're the new entry.
  - speaker: Reflection
    text: Oldest one in the Book. You just never turned to the back.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: How long have I been in this room?
  - speaker: Reflection
    text: Ask the radio.
  - speaker: Radio
    text: ...Caspian Air flight 214 to New York is now boarding. All passengers,
      please proceed to the gate.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: ...Huh. On time.
  endTitle: HOLLOW SAINT
  endSubtitle: 'Flight 214 to New York departed on schedule.

    Room 414 was found
    empty, the bed made, the mirror cold.'
  newspaperName: THE CASPIAN COURIER
  uiFont: {fileID: 0}
  osFontNames:
  - Georgia
  - Palatino Linotype
  - Times New Roman
